{"artifacts":{"architecture-governor.json":{"sha256":"d43c727a328c7286bcc1ff56e6688645a30b7e2507c52662e33c26e397413cb6","text":"{\"context_sha256\":\"b7a05ebea3df2504128c8297ff9b111db2a3abcdfc96e62711b2a7f22926a671\",\"contract_sha256\":\"d1954b999c4924965b9d23df7432fb94500f7038a64bb1160122b1b99c6b0673\",\"convergence\":\"improves\",\"debts\":[\"DEBT-CHAT-AREA\",\"DEBT-SIDEBAR\"],\"decision\":\"proceed\",\"design_sha256\":\"833a48e0278e7ce897fcf92ceb1ea007b82c8b77114be11021fcce58a799e834\",\"migrations\":[\"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS\"],\"policy_sha256\":\"0db30c9f1e05383df234c84feb31dcef348f09ec605db423606b9f72c7e54add\",\"principles\":[\"ARCH-DEEP-MODULES\",\"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES\"],\"rationale\":[\"The seam is named and unchanged: the fix lives entirely behind the existing useStreamingResponse(conversationId) interface; its return shape, startStream, and abortStream gain no new names, parameters, or configuration knobs.\",\"Deep-module compliant: the previous-id ref moves change detection inside the hook, so callers never orchestrate StrictMode or reset semantics and no send/reset orchestration leaks into ChatArea, the presentation component.\",\"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES respected: stream lifecycle and async orchestration stay in the hooks layer; no new dependency edge is created and no logic moves into components or pages.\",\"No-growth debts are untouched: planned_files exclude ChatArea.tsx and Sidebar.tsx, so the DEBT-CHAT-AREA and DEBT-SIDEBAR footprints cannot grow; MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS' direction (behavior in hooks, not large UI components) is followed, not fought.\",\"No parallel abstraction: the fix extends the established conversationId reset seam rather than adding a sibling hook or a second reset path beside it; the parallel reset-on-conversationId pattern in useMessages.ts is explicitly out of scope and untouched.\",\"The AC-3 guard survives: a previous-id sentinel treats the first mount for an id (and StrictMode's same-id second effect pass on the same component instance, which preserves refs) as not-a-change, while a genuine change to 'conv-b' or to null still aborts the old controller and clears all streaming state, keeping the existing reset suite and the #244 suite green.\",\"Testable through the interface: the one allowed new test file renders ChatArea under React.StrictMode with the real hook and a signal-honouring fetch mock, asserting observable behaviour (Stop response button, rendered assistant text) rather than private state, which is exactly how the seam should be proven.\",\"No cross-layer coupling added: backend, SSE wire format, src/lib/api.ts, and src/main.tsx are untouched per the contract's out-of-scope list, and the change requires no new imports beyond what the hook already has.\",\"Convergence improves rather than stays neutral because the reset contract becomes explicit and environment-independent ('abort and reset iff the conversation id genuinely changed') at constant interface width, where today correctness silently depends on React's effect-run count.\"],\"required_changes\":[],\"source_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-first-send-strictmode.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-refreshConversationsRef.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/VideoExplorer-admin-gate.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/VideoExplorer.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/adminApi.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatInput.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatInput.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Sidebar.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Sidebar.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/VideoExplorer.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useAdminVideos.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useAdminVideos.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useConversations.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useConversations.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useMessages.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/lib/api.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/main.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/pages/AdminVideos.tsx\"],\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"architecture-governor.raw.json":{"sha256":"6f89e79731066a460f01e1d5d268eacbb55952b47e5fee896394f7073d22f77f","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"decision\": \"proceed\",\n  \"convergence\": \"improves\",\n  \"principles\": [\"ARCH-DEEP-MODULES\", \"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES\"],\n  \"migrations\": [\"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS\"],\n  \"debts\": [\"DEBT-CHAT-AREA\", \"DEBT-SIDEBAR\"],\n  \"rationale\": [\n    \"The seam is named and unchanged: the fix lives entirely behind the existing useStreamingResponse(conversationId) interface; its return shape, startStream, and abortStream gain no new names, parameters, or configuration knobs.\",\n    \"Deep-module compliant: the previous-id ref moves change detection inside the hook, so callers never orchestrate StrictMode or reset semantics and no send/reset orchestration leaks into ChatArea, the presentation component.\",\n    \"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES respected: stream lifecycle and async orchestration stay in the hooks layer; no new dependency edge is created and no logic moves into components or pages.\",\n    \"No-growth debts are untouched: planned_files exclude ChatArea.tsx and Sidebar.tsx, so the DEBT-CHAT-AREA and DEBT-SIDEBAR footprints cannot grow; MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS' direction (behavior in hooks, not large UI components) is followed, not fought.\",\n    \"No parallel abstraction: the fix extends the established conversationId reset seam rather than adding a sibling hook or a second reset path beside it; the parallel reset-on-conversationId pattern in useMessages.ts is explicitly out of scope and untouched.\",\n    \"The AC-3 guard survives: a previous-id sentinel treats the first mount for an id (and StrictMode's same-id second effect pass on the same component instance, which preserves refs) as not-a-change, while a genuine change to 'conv-b' or to null still aborts the old controller and clears all streaming state, keeping the existing reset suite and the #244 suite green.\",\n    \"Testable through the interface: the one allowed new test file renders ChatArea under React.StrictMode with the real hook and a signal-honouring fetch mock, asserting observable behaviour (Stop response button, rendered assistant text) rather than private state, which is exactly how the seam should be proven.\",\n    \"No cross-layer coupling added: backend, SSE wire format, src/lib/api.ts, and src/main.tsx are untouched per the contract's out-of-scope list, and the change requires no new imports beyond what the hook already has.\",\n    \"Convergence improves rather than stays neutral because the reset contract becomes explicit and environment-independent ('abort and reset iff the conversation id genuinely changed') at constant interface width, where today correctness silently depends on React's effect-run count.\"\n  ],\n  \"required_changes\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Policy IDs are copied verbatim from the kernel-computed applicability set: ARCH-DEEP-MODULES and ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES prefix-overlap the planned files, MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS and DEBT-CHAT-AREA apply because ChatArea.tsx appears in context files, and DEBT-SIDEBAR because Sidebar.tsx appears in context files. Neither hotspot is in planned_files, which is precisely why the debts are satisfied; the implementer must resist 'while we are here' edits to ChatArea.tsx (e.g. touching dispatchedInitialRef or handleSend) since any growth there would trip the no-growth gate. Implementation caution: the sentinel should be an explicit unset marker (or initialize from the first observed id) rather than a run counter, so both the first-mount case and the change-to-null case behave per the invariants; refs persist across StrictMode's double effect invocation on the same instance, which is what makes the fix work. The design offers an alternative ('reset moved into the send path'); the previous-id-ref variant is architecturally preferable because it keeps the policy inside the hook, and design.json's data_flows already commit to it. The pinned red symptom and its exact-substring requirement are testing mechanics already owned by the contract's risks section, not architecture concerns, so they impose no structural demand here.\"\n}\n"},"context.enriched.json":{"sha256":"614339a6dc0d6473cafb17b38c4ba8731fac2fb7c2710c680d5f3de9a5037415","text":"{\"adrs\":[],\"callers\":[\"ChatArea.tsx#ChatArea\",\"ChatArea.tsx#handleSend\",\"ChatInput.tsx#ChatInput\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/Sidebar.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/VideoExplorer.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/hooks/useAdminVideos.ts\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/hooks/useConversations.ts\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/hooks/useMessages.ts\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.ts\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/main.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/pages/AdminVideos.tsx\"],\"contract_sha256\":\"d1954b999c4924965b9d23df7432fb94500f7038a64bb1160122b1b99c6b0673\",\"deterministic_impact\":{\"callers\":[\"app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"app/fron