ait, and the stop button's abortStream still aborts the in-flight stream on demand.\",\n    \"An intentional abort (user stop or a real navigation away) stays silent: the AbortError swallow branch in ChatArea.handleSend still produces no toast and no inline error.\",\n    \"Existing green suites remain green, notably the conversationId reset suite in app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.test.ts (reset on change and on change to null) and the #244 mid-stream-error suite.\",\n    \"A stream started on the current conversation survives StrictMode's mount-effect re-run: the first effect run for a conversation id (no previous value) is not treated as a change.\"\n  ],\n  \"adrs\": [],\n  \"history\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"No ADRs exist: docs/adr/ is absent and docs/agents/domain.md records the convention as dormant; docs/agents/*.md are process/domain docs, not architecture records. Mechanism confirmed in code: the reset effect at useStreamingResponse.ts:27-36 aborts streamAbortRef.current and clears state keyed on [conversationId]; it runs on every mount-effect pass, and startStream (useStreamingResponse.ts:61-62) installs the AbortController synchronously before its first await, so StrictMode's second pass aborts the in-flight first-message stream; ChatArea.tsx:532-534 silently swallows the resulting AbortError, so nothing renders. First-send wiring: ChatArea.tsx:575-583 dispatchedInitial effect reads location.state.initialMessage and calls handleSend, which routes to startStream when conversationId is set (ChatArea.tsx:462-517). Route topology (App.tsx:87-94, 113-120): /c/a -> /c/b keeps the same ConversationPage/AppLayout/ChatArea element mounted (prop change only), so the hook instance persists and a previous-id ref sees the genuine change — AC-3 holds without remount special-casing; / <-> /c/<id> genuinely remounts ChatArea, giving an uninitialized prev-id ref whose first run must count as not-a-change. The stop button is the ChatInput button with aria-label 'Stop response' (ChatInput.tsx:120-122), rendered only when isStreaming. Test constraints: existing ChatArea integration tests (ChatArea-refreshConversationsRef.test.tsx) mock useStreamingResponse out entirely, so the new StrictMode test must be a separate file using the REAL hook (the abort is only observable there); its useMessages mock must back setMessages with real React useState so the functional updater appends the assistant message and AC-2's rendered-text assertion can pass; React resolves to the development build under vitest (NODE_ENV=test) so React.StrictMode double-invokes effects for real; Element.prototype.scrollIntoView must be stubbed and ResizeObserver is absent in jsdom (guarded in ChatArea). The pinned red symptom requires findByRole('button', { name: 'Stop response' }) as the FIRST assertion and a fetch mock that honours init.signal (rejects with DOMException AbortError) on a gated ReadableStream SSE body. useMessages.ts carries the parallel reset-on-conversationId pattern but is explicitly out of scope, as is the stale streamingStatus?.tool read at useStreamingResponse.ts:166 (console.warn only).\"\n}\n"},"design.json":{"sha256":"833a48e0278e7ce897fcf92ceb1ea007b82c8b77114be11021fcce58a799e834","text":"{\"ac_mapping\":{\"AC-1\":[\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.ts#useStreamingResponse (conversationId reset effect)\"],\"AC-2\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleSend\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.ts#startStream\"],\"AC-3\":[\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.ts#useStreamingResponse (conversationId reset effect)\"]},\"allowed_new_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-first-send-strictmode.test.tsx\"],\"context_sha256\":\"b7a05ebea3df2504128c8297ff9b111db2a3abcdfc96e62711b2a7f22926a671\",\"contract_sha256\":\"d1954b999c4924965b9d23df7432fb94500f7038a64bb1160122b1b99c6b0673\",\"data_flows\":[\"location.state.initialMessage -> ChatArea send-on-mount effect -> ChatArea#handleSend -> useS